  "term": "Wernicke–Korsakoff syndrome",
  "definition": "Wernicke–Korsakoff syndrome is a disorder caused by thiamine deficiency. It most often occurs in people with alcoholism and involves confusion, problems with coordination, and paralysis or weakness of the eye muscles.",
